// Signing settings, kept out of the repository.
//
// The signing team is a property of the account building Pium, not of Pium.
// Hard-coding one here means every machine but the author's fails to build
// with "No signing certificate ... matching team ID" — a confusing error for
// something that is only ever a local setting.
//
// Create `Local.xcconfig` next to this file:
//
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID
//
// Find the ID in Xcode → Settings → Accounts, or read it from an installed
// certificate: `security find-certificate -c "Apple Development" -p \
// ~/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db | openssl x509 -noout -subject`
// prints it as the `OU` field.
//
// `#include?` is the optional form: a clone without `Local.xcconfig` builds
// rather than failing outright. Only the unit tests run unsigned, though —
// `PiumUITests` needs a real team, because the XCUITest runner refuses to load
// its own test bundle when the runner and the `.xctest` inside it were signed
// differently ("mapping process and mapped file have different Team IDs").
// That is also why this is set project-wide rather than per target.
//
// Release signing uses the Developer ID team and is configured separately in
// Phase 7.
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
